00:56:45.190 --> 00:56:56.030
<v Erick>I know that I'm hitting 10 because I'm gasping for air, rocking back and forth, and trying to induce a trance because there's nothing that's going to stop it.

00:56:56.030 --> 00:57:30.150
<v Ira Glass>I'm Ira Glass, back next week with more stories of This American Life.

00:57:30.150 --> 00:57:36.890
<v Ira Glass>Next week on the podcast of This American Life-- so this guy sits down with a woman, and he asks, are you recording this?

00:57:36.890 --> 00:57:38.230
<v Man>Are you recording this?

00:57:38.230 --> 00:57:39.670
<v Woman>No.

00:57:39.670 --> 00:57:44.670
<v Ira Glass>The thing is, though, the woman obviously is recording, and police are listening in. And she gets this guy to admit what he's done in detail, things she's wondered for years, in this recording. Here at our radio show, we have never heard anything like this. That's next week on the podcast or on your local public radio station.
